WEBVTT

00:03:58.621 --> 00:04:02.788
on on primates. So I've been interested
in what primates can teach us about

00:04:02.788 --> 00:04:04.954
leadership and how we all work together.

00:04:05.621 --> 00:04:07.538
And so I guess the place
I'd love to start

00:04:07.538 --> 00:04:11.288
on that is if you could just describe
some of your key insights

00:04:11.288 --> 00:04:14.746
and observations around when you
see primates collaborate.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.329
What does that teach you
about how humans work?

00:04:18.496 --> 00:04:24.579
Well, you know, the reason Dr. Leakey
sent me off to study chimpanzees in

00:04:24.579 --> 00:04:29.496
the first place is because he
spent his life searching for

00:04:29.496 --> 00:04:32.663
the fossilized remains
of Stone Age humans.